        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$18\\sqrt{21}\\text{ cm}^2$; height $=\\sqrt{15^2-6^2}=3\\sqrt{21}\\text{ cm}$.",
          "worked": "The altitude bisects the base. Let $h$ be the height in centimetres.\n$$\\begin{align*}h^2&=15^2-6^2\\\\h^2&=189\\\\h&=3\\sqrt{21}\\end{align*}$$\n$$\\begin{align*}A&=\\frac12\\times12\\times3\\sqrt{21}\\\\A&=18\\sqrt{21}\\text{ cm}^2\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 46
