        "answer": {
          "short": "$(12+2\\sqrt{161})\\text{ cm}$; height $=5\\sqrt5\\text{ cm}$ and each equal side $=\\sqrt{161}\\text{ cm}$.",
          "worked": "Let $h$ be the height and $s$ an equal side, in centimetres.\n$$\\begin{align*}30\\sqrt5&=\\frac12\\times12\\times h\\\\h&=5\\sqrt5\\end{align*}$$\nThe altitude bisects the base.\n$$\\begin{align*}s^2&=6^2+(5\\sqrt5)^2\\\\s^2&=161\\\\s&=\\sqrt{161}\\end{align*}$$\n$$\\begin{align*}P&=12+2s\\\\P&=(12+2\\sqrt{161})\\text{ cm}\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 57
