        "answer": {
          "short": "$30\\sqrt{13}\\text{ cm}^2$; each equal side is 19 cm and height $=5\\sqrt{13}\\text{ cm}$.",
          "worked": "Let $s$ be an equal side and $h$ the height, in centimetres.\n$$\\begin{align*}2s+12&=50\\\\s&=19\\end{align*}$$\nThe altitude bisects the base.\n$$\\begin{align*}h^2&=19^2-6^2\\\\h^2&=325\\\\h&=5\\sqrt{13}\\end{align*}$$\n$$\\begin{align*}A&=\\frac12\\times12\\times5\\sqrt{13}\\\\A&=30\\sqrt{13}\\text{ cm}^2\\end{align*}$$",
